================================================================================
                          THE SHORT VERSION
================================================================================

Take it. Run it. Fork it. Ship it. Sell it.

Leave the names on it, and pass the same freedom along.

That is the whole deal. Everything below is the machinery that makes it hold
up in a courtroom on any continent.


================================================================================
                          THE LICENSE STACK
================================================================================

This Work is distributed under FOUR instruments simultaneously. You receive the
rights of all of them; you must satisfy the obligations of the strictest.

  1. OPEN PIRACY LICENSE v1.1  ..............  LICENSES/OPL-1.1.txt
     The operative license. Carries the copyright grant, the database-right
     grant, the patent grant and retaliation clause, the moral-rights
     handling, the attribution requirements, the reciprocity (share-alike)
     obligation, the warranty disclaimer, the liability limits, and the
     termination-and-cure mechanism.

     This is the one that does the work. It is drafted to operate across
     common-law AND civil-law jurisdictions simultaneously — see its Preamble
     for why that distinction matters and what breaks without it.

  2. STREISAND ENGINE LICENSE v3.3  .........  LICENSES/SEL-3.3.txt
     A statement of philosophy and posture regarding suppression and
     replication. By its own terms it disclaims being a legal document. It is
     included because it is the project's declared position, not because it
     grants or disclaims anything operative.

  3. ROYAL WRIT OF THE SICILIAN CROWN  ......  LICENSES/ROYAL-WRIT-SICILIAN-CROWN.txt
     A declaratory instrument of standing, chain of title, and sovereignty,
     issued by H.M. Michael-Laurence: Curzi. It sits in the same tier as
     SEL-3.3 — a statement of position, not the operative software license.

     It carries ONE condition that does operate: MUTUAL SOVEREIGN RECOGNITION
     (Writ §1.2). Every user is recognised as a sovereign individual, and in
     taking that recognition must extend the identical recognition to every
     other individual. This is reciprocity, not discrimination — structurally
     the same move as share-alike, and it excludes no one. See Writ §1.3.

  4. CREATIVE COMMONS ATTRIBUTION-SHAREALIKE 4.0 INTERNATIONAL
     .........................................  LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
     Applies to documentation, specifications, diagrams, and other non-software
     content, at your option, in parallel with OPL-1.1.

     Canonical text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode


ORDER OF PRECEDENCE
-------------------
If they ever conflict about what you MAY or MUST do:

        OPL-1.1   >   CC BY-SA 4.0   >   Royal Writ   >   SEL-3.3

Where they differ in what they ALLOW, you get the union of the permissions.
Where they differ in what they REQUIRE, satisfy OPL-1.1 Article 3
(attribution), Article 4 (reciprocity), and Royal Writ §1.2 (mutual sovereign
recognition), and you have satisfied all of them.

See OPL-1.1 Article 12 for the full allocation rules.


ALLOCATION BY MATERIAL TYPE
---------------------------
    Software, firmware, HDL, build system     ->  OPL-1.1
    Documentation, specs, diagrams, media     ->  OPL-1.1 or CC BY-SA 4.0
    Everything, as a statement of position    ->  SEL-3.3, Royal Writ
    Mutual sovereign recognition (a term)     ->  Royal Writ §1.2


================================================================================
                          WHAT YOU MUST DO
================================================================================

Four things. That is all.

  1. KEEP THE NOTICES. Do not strip copyright headers or the NOTICE file.
     (OPL-1.1 Art. 3)

  2. SAY WHAT YOU CHANGED. If you ship a modified version, say so.
     (OPL-1.1 Art. 3.6)

  3. PASS IT ON. If you distribute a derived work, license it the same way and
     make the source available. (OPL-1.1 Art. 4)

  4. EXTEND WHAT YOU WERE EXTENDED. You are recognised as a sovereign
     individual; recognise everyone else as one too. Respect boundaries,
     keep divides symmetric, instrumentalise nobody.
     (Royal Writ §1.2, and src/concord/ where it is compiled)

You do NOT have to publish private modifications. You do NOT have to open
source your applications — calling ZXV's system calls, protocols, drivers, or
published libraries does not make your program a derived work. That boundary
is stated explicitly in OPL-1.1 Article 4.4 precisely because everyone else
left it ambiguous.


================================================================================
                       WHAT IS EXPRESSLY NOT GRANTED
================================================================================

  * TRADEMARKS. "ZEDEC", "ZEDEC XERO VULPINE", "ZXV", "VOVINA SHAKINA",
    "36N9 Genetics", and associated logos are not licensed. You may use them
    truthfully and descriptively ("built on ZXV"). You may not imply your fork
    is the official distribution. (OPL-1.1 Art. 6)

  * THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS. The Licensor grants only what the Licensor holds.
    (OPL-1.1 Art. 14.4)

  * ANY WARRANTY WHATSOEVER. This is an operating system and a cryptographic
    implementation. It is uncertified, unaudited, and not qualified for
    safety-critical use. Read OPL-1.1 Articles 8 and 10 before you rely on it
    for anything that matters.


================================================================================
                              CRYPTOGRAPHY
================================================================================

This Work contains cryptographic software (ML-KEM-768, X25519,
ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-GCM, Ed25519, SHA-256/SHA-3). Import, use, export and
re-export may be regulated where you are — Wassenaar, US EAR, EU 2021/821 and
national equivalents. Determining what applies to you is your responsibility.

The implementations are verified against published test vectors. That proves
interoperability and catches implementation error. It does NOT prove
resistance to side-channel attack, fault injection, or physical access, and
they have not been independently audited. (OPL-1.1 Art. 10)


================================================================================
                              CONTRIBUTING
================================================================================

Inbound equals outbound. Anything you submit is licensed under the same stack.
There is no CLA to sign and no copyright assignment — you keep your copyright,
and your name stays on your work exactly as ours stays on ours.
(OPL-1.1 Art. 7)


